  You're both right.  Nurse dancing is a deathtrap.  It can be done
successfully, but mostly only when it's no longer a big deal.  200+ hit
points is plenty to let you use an escape item.  200+ Hp also makes
nurse dancing a lot safer.

  Suggestions that you missed:

  - Speed up the nurse with /oSpeedMonster or !oSpeed
  - Speed up yourself with +oHasteSelf or !oSpeed
  - Be aware of other monsters by using:
    - light
    - Telepathy 
      - DANGEROUS if blinded.  Monsters can be generated next to you.
    - ESP
    - warning
    - b!oMonsterDetection (Underrated potion)
    - Spell of Monster Detection.
    Monsters are much less dangerous if you know they're coming.
  - Dance in confined areas
    - Sokoban with reverse geno
      - Its own special deathtrap if you don't strip beforehand.
      - Room on Medusa
      - Upper left hand room in Fort Ludios.
    - I've successfully danced
      - in the upper right hand corner of the VotD.
      - In a corner in Orcustown (two succubi and a nurse.  Who says 
        Anhur doesn't watch over fools?)
    - Close off openings with spell/wand of locking.


  Of course, if you're good enough to do all that, you're good enough
not to need the extra hitpoints.




